 "title": "A decade of tasks",
 "hook": "Between April 2009 and February 2019, software engineer Renzo Borgatti set 17,000+ daily tasks for himself. He completed slightly less than half of them. He labeled them with tags such as “@meeting”, “@talk”, and “@clojure”. He estimated how many “pomodoros” each would take, and how many they really did.",
